8 1 New Paragraph; Definitions; Tavern License. Amend RSA 175:1 by inserting after paragraph
9 LXIV-ccthefollowingnewparagraph:
10 LXIV-ccc. “Tavern license” means an on-premise license in an enclosed place of business
11 kept, used, maintained, advertised, and held out to the public as a place operated for the purpose of
12 servingliquorandbeverageswithoutthebenefitoffood.
13 2 New Sections; Tavern License. Amend RSA 178 by inserting after section 22 the following
14 newsections:
15 178:22-a TavernLicense.
16 I. The commission may issue a tavern license in any town which has voted to accept the
17 provisionsofRSA663:5,I(b),(c),and(d).
18 II. The license issued shall entitle the licensee to serve beverages or specialty beverages by
19 the glass, by the bottle with cap removed, or in any other suitable container, wines by the glass, by
20 the bottle with the cork or cap removed or in any other suitable container, or liquor by the glass or
21 othersuitablecontainer,asdefinedinrulesadoptedbythecommissionunderRSA541-A.
22 III. Nopersonundertheageof21shallbeallowedinthetavernlicensepremises.
23 IV. Except as provided in this paragraph, no beverages, specialty beverages, or liquor shall
24 beconsumedinthelicensedareasexceptthosethataresoldbythelicensee.
25 V. No beverages, specialty beverages, or liquor shall be removed from the licensed premises
26 bypatrons,exceptasprovidedbyRSA179:27-a.
27 178:22-b LocalOption.
28 I. Anytownorcitymayallow theoperationoftavernlicensesunderRSA178:21-aaccording
29 totheprovisionsofthissubdivision,inthefollowingmanner:
30 (a) In a town, the question shall be placed on the warrant of an annual town meeting
31 under the procedures set out in RSA 39:3, and shall be voted on a ballot. In a city, the legislative
32 bodymayvotetoplacethequestionontheofficialballotforanyregularmunicipalelection,or,inthe
